      "summary": ": Today at Cardrona Alpine Resort 26 Aug 2026 – Cardrona is open today and the winds have finally eased, though it won't stay calm for long — heavy snow is due to move in later this morning, with temperatures starting out mild before dropping through the day. It's shaping up as a proper stormy one, so expect visibility to drop and plenty of fresh snow to pile up on top of an overnight grooming effort. Main Basin and Valley View lead things off at 8:30am, with Captains, T-Bar and Soho following shortly after; Willows will have a delayed start. Kindy Conveyor, the Learner Conveyors, McDougall's Chondola, Whitestar Express, Captains Express, T-Bar, Soho Express and Willow's Quad are all turning, with only the Wells Pipe Platter closed. On the terrain side, Learners Slope, Main Basin, Captains, Soho, Little Willows, Big Willows and the Arcadia Chutes are open, while Mt Cardrona and the Summit are on hold as the storm rolls through — some further terrain closures are possible as the day develops, so keep an eye on signage. In the parks, Baby Bucks, Little Bucks, Antlers Alley, Stag Lane and Gravity Cross are open, with Big Bucks, Peoples Pipe, Olympic Pipe and Big Air currently closed. The Cardrona National Junior Champs GS race is running on Upper Goldrush today, so expect some closures around that. Chains are required on all vehicles from Valley View up, and there's an active hazard advisory on the access road worth checking before you head up.",
